# Performance overlay — apply AFTER pong_optimized.fragment
#
#   scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m .config \
#       patches/kernel-optimized/pong_optimized.fragment \
#       patches/kernel-optimized/pong_performance_overlay.fragment
#
# This is variant B of a deliberate A/B. Variant A (the base fragment alone)
# re-enables three cheap kernel mitigations that arter97 removes. This overlay
# puts them back the way he has them, so the build matches his hardening
# posture exactly and the two images differ ONLY in these three symbols.
#
# Why he removes them: they are his actual performance strategy — not
# `mitigations=off` (he leaves CPU mitigations ON), not `-O3` (he uses O2).
# Verified by reading his tree, not his embedded config.
#
# Rough cost of each, highest first:
#   INIT_STACK_ALL_ZERO  zeroes stack variables on every function entry —
#                        the expensive one, workload-dependent
#   SHADOW_CALL_STACK    separate return-address stack, reserves x18
#   HARDENED_USERCOPY    bounds-checks every copy_to/from_user
#
# Note CFI_CLANG and KASAN are already off in variant A, matching him, so
# they are not repeated here.
#
# Security cost is real: these are the cheapest exploit mitigations in the
# kernel. Run this variant only if the speed difference is one you can
# actually perceive — otherwise variant A is the better daily driver.

# CONFIG_INIT_STACK_ALL_ZERO is not set
CONFIG_INIT_STACK_NONE=y
# CONFIG_SHADOW_CALL_STACK is not set
# CONFIG_HARDENED_USERCOPY is not set
